---
import Base from '../../layouts/Base.astro';
const scenarios = ['Aviation dispatch & diversion', 'Robot trajectory safety', 'GNSS integrity', 'Order book risk', 'GPU cooling & thermal incidents', 'Macro volatility shocks', 'Satellite RF degradation'];
---
<Base title="Decision Intelligence Engine" description="An interactive Gradio application exploring structured decision routing, telemetry inputs, and confidence gates across seven scenarios."><div class="container page-shell">
<a class="text-link" href="/projects/">← All projects</a>
<section class="project-opening"><div class="eyebrow">FEATURED PROJECT / INTERACTIVE APPLICATION</div><h1 class="page-title">Decision Intelligence<br /><em>Engine.</em></h1><p class="page-intro">An interactive control room for exploring how telemetry becomes a structured decision: a selected action, a risk signal, and a severity score.</p><div class="tags large"><span>Python</span><span>Gradio</span><span>NumPy</span><span>Matplotlib</span><span>OpenRouter</span><span>TypeSafe SDK</span></div><div class="button-row"><a class="button primary" href="#application">Try the application ↓</a><a class="button secondary" href="https://huggingface.co/spaces/jacobroutzong/decision-intelligence-engine" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Open Hugging Face ↗</a><a class="text-link" href="https://github.com/jacobhroutzong/decision-intelligence-engine" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">View source ↗</a></div></section>
<section class="project-story"><div><div class="eyebrow">01 / THE IDEA</div><h2>Make the decision<br />process visible.</h2></div><div><p>The application puts telemetry inputs, model outputs, and a configurable confidence threshold into one interface. You can change a scenario’s inputs, run an evaluation, and inspect both the visual result and its JSON audit record.</p><p>The routing path calls Liquid AI’s <code>liquid/d1-ultra</code> through OpenRouter using the TypeSafe SDK. The interface exposes categorical choice, binary risk, and ordinal severity outputs together.</p></div></section>
<section class="project-story"><div><div class="eyebrow">02 / EXPLORE THE INTERFACE</div><h2>From inputs<br />to inspection.</h2></div><ol class="walkthrough"><li><h3>Choose a scenario</h3><p>Start with aviation dispatch or explore robotics, infrastructure, navigation, and market risk examples.</p></li><li><h3>Adjust the telemetry</h3><p>Each scenario has three sliders with domain-specific units. A separate slider controls the confidence gate.</p></li><li><h3>Inspect the result</h3><p>Review the selected route, confidence, risk signal, severity, measured request latency, and choice probability chart.</p></li><li><h3>Read the audit record</h3><p>Compare the serialized input with the JSON output to understand what the interface sent and received.</p></li></ol></section>
<section class="scenario-section"><div class="eyebrow">03 / SCENARIOS</div><h2>Seven ways to explore the same pipeline.</h2><div class="scenario-grid">{scenarios.map((scenario,index) => <div><span class="mono">{String(index+1).padStart(2,'0')}</span><h3>{scenario}</h3></div>)}</div></section>
<section id="application" class="application-section"><div class="section-heading"><div><div class="eyebrow">04 / THE APPLICATION</div><h2>Explore it here.</h2></div><a class="text-link" href="https://huggingface.co/spaces/jacobroutzong/decision-intelligence-engine" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Open full screen ↗</a></div><p>Load the Hugging Face application below to keep exploring within the portfolio. If the Space is waking up or the embed is unavailable, use the full-screen link.</p><div class="embed-shell"><div id="app-placeholder"><h3>Decision Intelligence Engine</h3><p>Hosted on Hugging Face Spaces. Loading the app connects your browser to Hugging Face; it does not run an evaluation.</p><button id="load-app" class="button primary">Load interactive application</button></div><iframe id="project-app" title="Decision Intelligence Engine interactive application" data-src="https://jacobroutzong-decision-intelligence-engine.hf.space" loading="lazy" referrerpolicy="strict-origin-when-cross-origin" hidden></iframe></div><p class="small muted">Evaluations use the Space’s configured provider credentials or its API-key override field. No credentials are collected by this portfolio.</p></section>
<section class="project-story"><div><div class="eyebrow">05 / CURRENT SCOPE</div><h2>What this version<br />demonstrates.</h2></div><div><p>The telemetry router is connected to a model API. Its calibration tab currently uses seeded synthetic confidence and outcome data; the throughput tab generates simulated latencies. Those charts illustrate evaluation concepts and are not measured model benchmarks.</p><p>The scenarios are software demonstrations. This application does not operate aircraft, robots, trading systems, or physical infrastructure. Gate labels describe the interface’s threshold logic.</p><p>Source reviewed October 18, 2026. The independently hosted Space can change as the project develops.</p><a class="text-link" href="https://huggingface.co/spaces/jacobroutzong/decision-intelligence-engine/tree/main" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Explore the Space implementation ↗</a></div></section>
</div></Base>
<script>
const loadButton = document.querySelector<HTMLButtonElement>('#load-app');
loadButton?.addEventListener('click', () => {
 const frame = document.querySelector<HTMLIFrameElement>('#project-app');
 const placeholder = document.querySelector<HTMLElement>('#app-placeholder');
 if (!frame?.dataset.src) return;
 frame.src = frame.dataset.src;
 frame.hidden = false;
 if (placeholder) placeholder.hidden = true;
});
</script>
